# The headers Cloudflare sends with every file it serves from the build (wrangler.jsonc `assets`;
# the server's /api/* and /ws/* answers, which reach the Worker first, are not files). The CSP's
# `connect-src` names the build's own hosts, so the build fills its placeholder in (static-pages.ts
# `connectSources`): 'self', the build's VITE_SUPABASE_URL with Google Identity Services' requests
# (R2983000, below), and wss:// on the build's own host. It fails on a placeholder it leaves.
# apps/web/src/net/cloudflare-config.test.ts holds this file.
# R2983000: Google's own sign-in button (Google Identity Services, on /login) needs its script, its
# frames, its styles and its requests (static-pages.ts `GOOGLE_IDENTITY_SOURCE`), and nothing else.
# R3507000: `img-src` also names Roblox's one image host (auth/LinkedAccounts.tsx shows a linked Roblox
# account's headshot from it; net/auth.ts `ROBLOX_AVATAR_IMAGE_HOST`), and no wildcard.
# #3485: Strict-Transport-Security pairs with Always Use HTTPS (infra/cloudflare.tf). It ships to
# staging and *.workers.dev deliberately: all are HTTPS-only, and promote-production.yml's live check
# (bundle content, /decks 200, a Content-Security-Policy header, /not-a-page 404) asserts nothing it
# breaks. No `preload`: the domain was never submitted.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/client; worker-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://tr.rbxcdn.com; media-src 'self' blob:; font-src 'self'; frame-src 'self' https://accounts.google.com/gsi/; connect-src %CONNECT_SRC%; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# The web fonts (src/fonts.css): a file's name carries its version, so a browser keeps it a year.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The bundle, its chunks and the engine's module (Vite's build output): every name carries its content's hash, so a browser keeps it a year (#778).
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
